# Coding Standards

## Formatting (`.editorconfig`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`)
- MUST indent with **4 spaces**; NEVER use tabs
- MUST place opening brace on same line: `if (x) {`
- MUST insert final newline; MUST trim trailing whitespace (except `*.md`)
- MUST run `npm run lint` in `client/` before submitting TS/HTML changes

## TypeScript (`client/`, ESLint)
- MUST use `interface` for object shapes (`@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-definitions`)
- MUST remove unused imports (`unused-imports/no-unused-imports`)
- MUST wrap multi-line `if/for/while` bodies in braces (`curly: multi-line`)
- MUST prefix Angular selectors with `app` (kebab-case elements, camelCase directives)
- MUST NOT introduce `any` without inline justification comment

## JavaScript (`server/`)
- MUST start files with `'use strict';`
- MUST use `require()` / `module.exports` (CommonJS); no ES modules in server runtime
- MUST use 4-space indent matching existing files in the same directory
- MUST use `var`/`function` style when editing existing files; do not mass-convert to `const`

## Naming
| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Angular component | `*.component.ts` | `alarm-view.component.ts` |
| Angular service | `*.service.ts` in `_services/` | `project.service.ts` |
| Server API module | `server/api/<name>/index.js` | `alarms/index.js` |
| Device driver | `server/runtime/devices/<proto>/index.js` | `modbus/index.js` |
| Test file | `<subject>.test.js` | `jwtLifecycleSecurity.test.js` |

## Error Handling & Logging
- Server errors MUST use `server/runtime/logger.js` (Winston), not bare `console.log` in production paths
- API handlers MUST return HTTP status codes (4xx/5xx); NEVER swallow auth failures silently
- Angular services MUST surface user-facing errors via `ToastrService` or `TranslateService`

## Comments
- MUST NOT add comments that restate obvious code
- MUST add comments only for non-obvious protocol behavior, security checks, or SCADA edge cases
